From: ARLinux contributors
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase: cover WoW64 WebView2 launchers on ARM64

A 32-bit WebView2 host can launch the 64-bit browser through WoW64. Its
initial command line is assembled by the i386 kernelbase, not the ARM64EC
one. Apply GE's existing WebView2 sandbox compatibility entry there too.
Otherwise Chromium tries to install x64 interception thunks into ARM64X
Wine builtins and aborts with SBOX_ERROR_CANNOT_SETUP_INTERCEPTION_THUNK.
This does not disable GPU acceleration or alter other browser arguments.

diff --git a/dlls/kernelbase/process.c b/dlls/kernelbase/process.c
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/process.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/process.c
@@ -602,3 +602,3 @@
-#if defined(__aarch64__) || defined(__arm64ec__)
+#if defined(__aarch64__) || defined(__arm64ec__) || defined(__i386__)
         {L"msedgewebview2.exe", L" --no-sandbox"},
 #endif
